{%- comment -%}
  Renders the "Due separately to National Gym Service" summary in the cart and
  the cart drawer, and nothing at all when the cart holds no NGS service.

  Where the selections come from. The chosen options are NOT separate cart
  lines. The Cart Transform expands the bundle further down the funnel, so
  `cart.items` holds only the parent variant and the customer's choices live on
  that line's private `_functionOperation` property. Shopify exposes that
  property to Liquid already parsed, as an array of hashes with `variantId`,
  `quantity` and `priceAdjustment`, so it can be walked directly. An earlier
  revision treated it as a string and matched nothing.

  Where the amount comes from. Not from the cart line price. Once the Cart
  Transform that defers these services is deployed the NGS component sits at
  $0.00, so reading line prices would report nothing owed. The amount is taken
  from the same trusted `fs_bundle.ngs_allowlist` shop metafield the function
  and the PDP read, which holds the approved amount per variant. The figure is
  therefore correct both before and after that deployment, and a customer
  cannot influence it by editing the posted payload.

  Accepts:
    - context: {String} 'drawer' or 'page', used only for the wrapper class.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign ngs_options = shop.metafields.fs_bundle.ngs_allowlist.value.options -%}

{%- if ngs_options.size > 0 and cart.item_count > 0 -%}
  {%- assign ngs_total_cents = 0 -%}
  {%- assign ngs_line_count = 0 -%}

  {%- for item in cart.items -%}
    {%- for property in item.properties -%}
      {%- if property.first == '_functionOperation' -%}
        {%- for selection in property.last -%}
          {%- assign selected_id = selection.variantId | split: '/' | last -%}
          {%- for entry in ngs_options -%}
            {%- assign entry_id = entry.variantId | split: '/' | last -%}
            {%- if entry_id == selected_id -%}
              {%- assign units = selection.quantity | default: 1 | times: item.quantity -%}
              {%- assign line_cents = entry.price | times: 100 | times: units -%}
              {%- assign ngs_total_cents = ngs_total_cents | plus: line_cents -%}
              {%- assign ngs_line_count = ngs_line_count | plus: 1 -%}
              {%- break -%}
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  {%- endfor -%}

  {%- if ngs_line_count > 0 -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      Styles live with the snippet so the block looks the same in the drawer and
      on the cart page without depending on which stylesheet either surface
      happens to load. Matches the PDP block in .ngs-due-line.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <style>
      .ngs-cart-summary {
        margin: 12px 0 0;
        padding: 10px 12px;
        background-color: #eef4fb;
        border: 1px solid #b9d2ea;
        border-radius: 8px;
        font-family: 'Lato', sans-serif;
        font-size: 14px;
        line-height: 20px;
        color: #23232b;
        text-align: left;
      }
      .ngs-cart-summary__row {
        display: flex;
        align-items: baseline;
        justify-content: space-between;
        gap: 8px;
      }
      .ngs-cart-summary__label { font-weight: 700; }
      .ngs-cart-summary__value {
        font-weight: 700;
        color: #1c4e80;
        white-space: nowrap;
      }
      .ngs-cart-summary__note {
        margin: 6px 0 0;
        font-size: 13px;
        line-height: 18px;
        color: #4a4a55;
      }
    </style>
    <div class="ngs-cart-summary ngs-cart-summary--{{ context | default: 'page' }}" data-ngs-cart-summary>
      <div class="ngs-cart-summary__row">
        <span class="ngs-cart-summary__label">Due separately to National Gym Service:</span>
        <span class="ngs-cart-summary__value" data-ngs-cart-total>{{ ngs_total_cents | money }}</span>
      </div>
      <p class="ngs-cart-summary__note">
        {%- if ngs_line_count == 1 -%}
          This service is
        {%- else -%}
          These {{ ngs_line_count }} services are
        {%- endif %}
        not billed today by Fitness Superstore. National Gym Service LLC will
        contact you after your order to arrange payment. Installation is
        scheduled, and a paid extended warranty starts, once that payment is
        confirmed.
      </p>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
